-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  suite_cli_help_build.adam - `adam help build` (no banner): build's usage,
  summary, the options that belong to it (its own -o, no "only" tag) and
  its examples, exit 0
*******************************************************************************/

/*
@@test
  kind cli
  args "--no-banner" "help" "build"
  exitcode 0
  | USAGE:
  |   adam build [<file|folder>] [options]
  |
  | Build the program whose main module is <file>, or the project whose project.toml is in <folder> (default: the current folder), into an exe
  |
  | OPTIONS:
  |   -o, --output     <dir>     The output folder: build writes the exe to its bin (else the main module's @outputpath, else its project's output folder, else output under the working folder); cimport writes the unit into it (else the spec's output folder, else the spec's own)
  |   -t, --target     <target>  The target, by its name or its triple (TARGETS lists them); wins over the main module's @target
  |   -opt, --optimize <level>   The optimization level: debug, safe, fast or small; wins over the main module's @optimize
  |   -r, --run                  Run the exe once built, in its folder; the arguments after -- are its own
  |   -d, --debug                Debug the exe once built, in this console (h lists the debugger's commands); the arguments after -- are its own
  |   --emit-ir                  Also write <name>.ir beside the exe: the optimized IR of the program's own units, with each function's analysis
  |   --no-banner                Print no banner: for scripts and tests
  |   -q, --quiet                Print only the reports: no banner, no phase or status lines (scripts, tests)
  |   -h, --help                 Show the help of the command given (else adam's)
  |
  | TARGETS:
  |   win64                      x86_64-windows-gnu (default)
  |
  | EXAMPLES:
  |   adam build hello.adam
  |   adam build hello.adam -o bin
  |   adam build myproject
@@end
*/

module exe suite_cli_help_build;

begin
end.
